we need more women entrepreneurs we need  more women in business find your passion  and really get behind it and and don't  give up there's so many times when it  seems insurmountable but if you have the  wherewithal to keep the hard work going  and and really understand that you can  make a difference it's well worth it a  friend of mine when I first did my first  article in The New York Times she called  me up Jane Rosenthal and said the  article is great but you shied away from  the word ambition and you should never  ever shy away from that word again and I  think that's great advice for women I  think women should be just as ambitious  as men and be proud of it from the  fashion standpoint I think it's very  important to have a unique point of view  and there's a lot of competition and  it's a saturated market and I think that  if there's always room for great  companies if it's different and you have  your own point of view and a unique  style and and that's what I think you  have to focus on is the end of the day  it's about the product it has to be  great and it has to be different and not  too referential of what else is out  there  one thing that we speak a lot about in  our company regardless of the tremendous  growth we have had is restraint and I  have never regretted saying no to  something whether it's different  collaborations or partnerships or  opening a store or whatever it may be we  we are a very patient company and we  want to always look to the long-term so  when I talk to entrepreneurs I always  speak about that and say how important  it is to really think forward and and  not just take what comes along and  really be thoughtful in building your  business
 

